{{Quote|Rey, be brave.|Miramir|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
'''Miramir''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who worked as a [[Junk dealer|junk trader]] during the [[New Republic Era]]. Her [[Marriage|husband]] [[Dathan]] was the [[Cloning|cloned]] "son"&mdash;an [[Bioengineering|artificial]] [[Strand-Cast]]&mdash;of [[Darth Sidious]], the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] and [[Galactic Emperor]]. Miramir had a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Youngling|child]] with Dathan, a daughter named [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], who was [[Reproduction|born]] in [[15 ABY]]. Though Miramir's husband lacked the ability to use [[the Force]], Rey was born [[Force-sensitive]] as a result of her [[Parent|father's]] [[DNA|genetic]] connection to the [[Palpatine family|Palpatine bloodline]].

Despite their family's connection to the Dark [[Lord]] of the [[Sith]], Miramir and Dathan chose to live as anonymous junk traders on the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Jakku]]. They succeeded in hiding Rey from Sidious, who intended to use Rey as a [[Transference|vessel]] for his spirit, by leaving her on Jakku with [[Unkar Plutt]]. Miramir and her husband were subsequently captured and [[Death|killed]] by the [[Sith assassin]] [[Ochi]], whom the [[Emperor]] had sent to retrieve his granddaughter.

==Biography==
===Early life===
Miramir was [[Reproduction|born]] on the [[planet]] [[Hyperkarn]]<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> in [[6 BBY]].<ref name="Birth date" /> [[Gender|She]] lived with her [[Miramir's grandmother|grandmother]], whom she was very close with.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" />

===The birth of Rey===
{{Quote|When he sired a genetic heir to my Empire, a new opportunity to ensure my legacy arose. But my errant clone and his mate absconded with their child and went into hiding.|Darth Sidious|<ref name="Secrets of the Sith">''[[Star Wars: Secrets of the Sith]]''</ref>}}
During the [[New Republic Era|rise]] of the [[New Republic]], Miramir<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> married [[Dathan]], the [[Cloning|cloned]] "son"&mdash;a [[DNA|genetic]] [[Strand-Cast|strandcast]]&mdash;of [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious]]. The [[Emperor]] had not anticipated the relationship between his clone and Miramir, but through it he sought to continue his [[blood]]line the [[Reproduction|natural]] way after [[Bioengineering|genetic experimentation]] on his [[Clone template|template]] failed to produce a viable host for his essence. When their daughter, [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], was born<ref name="TROS EE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> in [[15 ABY]],<ref name="Rey date">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]'' states that Rey is nineteen [[Standard year|years]] old during the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], which is dated to [[34 ABY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''. Therefore it can be deduced that Rey was [[Reproduction|born]] in [[15 ABY]].</ref> she inherited her [[Palpatine family|grandfather's]] [[Force-sensitive|connection]] to [[the Force]], whereas her [[Parent|father]] had not.<ref name="TROS EE" />

Miramir gave birth to their daughter on her home world but soon left with Dathan; they fled to Jakku where they would live in obscurity for six years,<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> struggling to survive as junk traders<ref name="TROS EE" /> and [[moisture farmer]]s.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> 

===Exile and death===
{{Quote|She isn't on Jakku. She's gone.|Miramir, to Ochi|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:Rey_mum_and_dad-TROS.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Rey's parents left her on Jakku to prevent Darth Sidious from finding her.]]
The Emperor intended to [[Transference|transfer his spirit]] to his granddaughter's body, leaving the unstable cloned body that could not sustain his power in the [[dark side of the Force]]. However, his plan was thwarted by Rey's parents, who escaped into hiding along with their daughter. Sidious sent his devotee, the [[assassin]] [[Ochi]], after them,<ref name="TROS EE" /> determined to regain his granddaughter and "punish" her parents who, in his view, betrayed him.<ref name="Secrets of the Sith" /> They eventually settled on [[Jakku]], having elected to live in obscurity on a [[desert]] [[planet]] in order to keep their daughter safe.<ref name="TROS EE" />

Life on Jakku was difficult for Rey's family, her mother and father struggling to survive as [[Junk dealer|junk traders]].<ref name="TROS EE" /> Their efforts to hide Rey were nearly compromised when Ochi drew closer to locating them. In an act of desperation, they departed Jakku aboard Ochi's ship, the ''[[Bestoon Legacy]]'', and left their daughter with [[Unkar Plutt]], paying Plutt with Dathan's [[songsteel]] [[Unidentified amulet|Sith amulet]].<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Miramir embraced her daughter for the last time, her face partly obscured by a [[Color|blue]] [[Clothing|shawl]].<ref name="TROS Junior Novel">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> Miramir also took some [[Aki-Aki]] beads that were in Plutts possession in hopes of using them to trick Ochi in case he caught them.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Rey watched as the ''Bestoon Legacy'' departed from Jakku. Knowing her parents were onboard the [[transport]], she tried to free herself from Plutt's grasp while screaming for her parents to not leave her behind.<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" />

[[File:Reys_Parents.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Sidious had Miramir and Dathan killed for refusing to reveal their daughter's location.]]
Miramir and Dathan were subsequently caught and taken as [[prisoner]]s by Ochi.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Ochi interrogated the couple regarding their daughter's whereabouts, Miramir tried to undermine Ochi's investigation with misinformation, claiming that Rey was not on Jakku and that she was simply gone. Her lie was unacceptable to Sidious' follower; acting on his master's command, he used his [[Blade of Ochi of Bestoon|dagger]] to stab Dathan and then Miramir to [[death]].<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> As she had predicted, Ochi was tricked by the Aki-Aki beads and traveled to the planet [[Pasaana]].<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Due to Ochi's subsequent death on Pasaana, Rey remained hidden from her grandfather and the [[Sith Eternal]] [[Sith cultist|cult]] that supported him.<ref name="TROS EE" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|I never lied to you. Your parents were no one. They chose to be to keep you safe.|Kylo Ren, to Rey|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:Rey_AT-AT.png|thumb|left|250px|Rey grew up as a scavenger on Jakku, hoping to be reunited with her mother and father one day.]]
The bodies of Rey's parents were found stuffed in a crate and drifting in space by [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] and [[R2-D2]], who recovered them and took them to the frozen world of [[Neftali]] where they [[Burial|buried]] them with the help of [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Komat]]. Having died holding the Aki-Aki beads she'd obtained from Plutt, Miramir successfully led Ochi to the incorrect conclusion that they had left Rey on [[Pasaana]], leading him to go there in search of her. Upon landing there Ochi began seeing [[hallucination]]s of Miramir and Dathan, and his search for Rey on the world was short lived, soon sinking in the world's [[quicksand]] shortly after leaving his ship<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> where he remained until his death.<ref name="Episode IX" />

Though Rey had all but forgotten her past, she remained on Jakku for [[Standard year|years]] in the hope of reuniting with her mother and father.<ref name="TROS EE" /> During that time, she had nightmares of Miramir and Dathan abandoning her when she was a child.<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> That memory resurfaced several times, once when she visited [[Takodana]],<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> the second shortly after her escape from the ''[[Supremacy]]'',<ref name="TLJ Junior novel">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> and the third during her [[Jedi training]] on [[Ajan Kloss]]. Following the third occurrence, however, she remembered another forgotten moment from her childhood, in which she found herself in the warm embrace of a woman that she knew to be her mother.<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" />

Rey was [[Battle of Takodana|captured on Takodana]] by the [[First Order]] [[warlord]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], who learned about the [[scavenger]]'s parents through the [[Force-bond]] that connected their [[Brain|minds]]. Based on what he saw of them through a [[Force vision]], Ren concluded that Rey was sired by insignificant<ref name="TROS EE" /> junk traders.<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref> The desperate conditions of their lives also convinced Ren that they abandoned their daughter,<ref name="TROS EE" /> selling Rey for drinking money, and that they were dead and buried in a pauper's grave in the [[desert]] of Jakku.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

[[File:DaveOFlanagan-JediMaster.png|thumb|right|300px|As a Jedi, Rey journeyed to Exegol to destroy Sidious, her paternal "grandfather" (biological uncle) who had her parents killed.]]
Rey's mother was remembered by Sidious as the wife of his clone, whom he despised as a "useless creature" that he rejected due to its powerlessness in the Force.<ref name="Secrets of the Sith" /> The Emperor revealed to Ren the secret of Rey's lineage as his granddaughter. The revelation did not change Ren's mind about Rey's parents; he still regarded them as nonentities. Nevertheless, he tried to turn Rey to the dark side by telling her that Sidious, her grandfather, ordered her parents' execution. Ren's actions caused Rey to rediscover forgotten memories of her childhood, including the last time she saw her parents.<ref name="TROS EE" /> Though she possessed qualities of a Jedi,<ref name="Secrets of the Sith" /> Rey struggled to resist the seduction of the dark side. The knowledge that her mother and father were killed on her grandfather's orders caused Rey to develop a desire to avenge them. Ultimately, though, the memory of her parents kept Rey entrenched in the [[light side of the Force]]. During the [[Battle of Exegol]], Rey succeeded in destroying her grandfather, preventing the rebirth of the [[Sith]].<ref name="TROS EE" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Weak. Like your parents.''"<br />"''My parents were strong. They saved me from you.|Darth Sidious and Rey|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:DathanReyMiramir-CGSWG.png|thumb|left|250px|Rey was loved by her mother, who endured a life of hardship and sacrifice for her daughter's sake.]]
Miramir was a young<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who had blonde [[hair]], brown [[eye]]s, and light skin. Like her husband, she loved Rey and was willing to risk death by hiding her daughter from [[Darth]] Sidious.<ref name="Episode IX" /> She chose to live in obscurity to keep Rey safe and bore the consequences of her choice, living [[Standard day|day]]-to-day on the edge of desperation.<ref name="TROS EE" /> With Ochi on her trail,<ref name="Episode IX" /> she made the heart-breaking decision<ref name="Space Moms">{{InsiderCite|221|Space Moms}}</ref> to leave behind her daughter, though not before embracing her one last time, telling Rey to be brave.<ref name="Episode IX" />

Having to give her daughter away, even to keep her safe, drove Rey's mother to tears as they embraced for the final time, neither one wanting to let the other go.<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> She remained defiant during her final moments, refusing to reveal her daughter's whereabouts to the Emperor's hunter even when her life and that of her husband were threatened. Though dismissed as unimportant and weak by Ren and Sidious, Miramir was remembered by Rey as someone who was strong enough to keep her daughter safe from her grandfather.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Behind the scenes==
Miramir first appeared, albeit unseen, in the [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novelization)|novelization]] of the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. In the novel, during the sequence depicting Rey's force vision on Takodana, she hears a voice say "Stay here. I'll come back for you," and "I'll come back, sweetheart, I promise."<ref name="FAnovel">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novelization)|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' novelization]]</ref> The [[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel|junior novelization]] for the following film [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] would incorporate a scene during the events of the film where Rey has a dream of that same voice uttering the same lines once again.<ref name="TLJ Junior">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> Miramir would go on to be depicted in live action in a flashback sequence in the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], where she was portrayed by [[Jodie Comer]].<ref name="Episode IX" /> She was finally identified in the [[2022]] novel ''[[Shadow of the Sith]]'' by [[Adam Christopher]].<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" />

''Shadow of the Sith'' affirmed that the words Rey had heard in the vision in ''The Force Awakens'' novelization were actually part of her last meeting with Miramir, taking place during the sequence where Dathan and Miramir bid farewell to her.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> ''The Rise of Skywalker'' also sees Kylo Ren claim Mirarmir and Dathan sold Rey off to keep her safe,<ref name="Episode IX" /> but ''Shadow of the Sith'' instead revealed that she and her husband paid to keep Rey safe.<ref name="Paid with Songsteel">{{Twitter|ghostfinder|status/1720061820998762702|[[Adam Christopher]]|quote=Rey wasn't sold to Unkar Plutt - Dathan and Miramir paid him with a songsteel medallion to hide her.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Dmreo}}</ref> Christopher named the character after [[Wikipedia:Miramar, New Zealand|Miramar]], a suburb of [[Wikipedia:Wellington|Wellington]], [[Wikipedia:New Zealand|New Zealand]]. According to the author, he wanted a fantasy name to go with Miramir's [[homeworld]] [[Hyperkarn]], which is mysterious and has a twilight forest. The author typed in the name and switched around some of the letters, and thought the name Miramir had a magical quality, almost Elven.<ref name="CNET">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cnet.com/culture/entertainment/star-wars-shadow-of-the-sith-makes-luke-skywalker-the-most-powerful-person-in-the-galaxy|text='Star Wars: Shadow of the Sith' Makes Luke Skywalker 'The Most Powerful Person in The Galaxy|author=Sean Keane|date=2022-09-05|quote=With Miramir, I wanted a kind of fantasy name, because in the book we see her home planet -- it's not magical, but it has a twilight forest and is very mysterious. There's a place in Wellington in New Zealand called Miramar, which is where Weta Studios, who made Lord of the Rings, are based. I just typed it in, switched some of the letters and I was like "Well hang on -- that sounds really cool." It had a kind of magical quality, it sounds almost Elven. It was also a contrast to Dathan, which is relatively simple. Whereas Miramir sounds a little bit otherworldly. |work=''[[Wikipedia:CNET|CNET]]''|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/dVM71|archivedate=2022-09-07}}</ref> According to the author, Miramir is pronounced "Mirr - Ah - Meer."<ref name="Christopher Twitter">{{Twitter|ghostfinder|status/1527363213087903747|[[Adam Christopher]]|date=2022-05-19|quote=Pronunciation guide: Dathan as in Nathan. Miramir is Mirr - Ah - Meer. If you're lucky I might reveal the origins at my #StarWarsCelebration panel...|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/pM5Ji|archivedate=2022-09-07}}</ref> Christopher has stated he is emotionally moved by her and Dathan's brief appearances in ''The Rise of Skywalker'' every time he watches the film.<ref name="Emotional">{{Twitter|ghostfinder|status/1851558968587350432|[[Adam Christopher]]|quote=Dathan and Miramir’s fleeting appearance in The Rise of Skywalker chokes me up each time, and I’m the one who wrote the bloody book!|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/XV0Li}}</ref>

